# Project structure

Human-readable mirror: [docs/01-overview/PROJECT_LAYOUT.md](../../docs/01-overview/PROJECT_LAYOUT.md) (keep in sync when layout changes).

- **Top-level layout**
  - `minecraftmod/` is the Gradle root for this mod (`settings.gradle` includes subprojects).
  - **`api`** — outward-facing Java API (interop surfaces); no Clojure game logic.
  - **`mcmod`** — platform-neutral foundation: protocols, DSLs, metadata, utilities (no Forge/Fabric/NeoForge or `net.minecraft.*`).
  - **`ac`** — platform-neutral game content and domain logic; depends on `mcmod` only (plus `api` where needed).
  - **`:platform`** — single catalog-driven platform project. Select a target with `scripts/target-gradle.ps1 <target-id>`; do **not** add root `forge-1.20.1/` / `fabric-1.20.1/` / `neoforge-1.21.1/` Gradle modules.

- **Platform source (`platform-src/`, assembled by `platform-catalog.json`)**
  - **`minecraft/base/`** — `minecraft-base` component (`cn.li.mcbase.*`): version-agnostic Minecraft glue (entity specs, platform ops, runtime SPIs, datagen helpers). Must not reference `cn.li.mc1201` / `cn.li.mc1211`.
  - **`minecraft/mc-1.20.1/`** — `minecraft-1.20.1` (`cn.li.mc1201.*` + `cn.li.mcver.*` downgrade seam).
  - **`minecraft/mc-1.21.1/`** — `minecraft-1.21.1` (`cn.li.mc1211.*` + `cn.li.mcver.*` contract-shaped seam).
  - **`loader/forge-1.20.1/`** — Forge entrypoints, `mods.toml`, events, registration (`cn.li.forge1201.*`).
  - **`loader/fabric-1.20.1/`** — Fabric entrypoints, `fabric.mod.json`, events (`cn.li.fabric1201.*`).
  - **`loader/neoforge-1.21.1/`** — NeoForge entrypoints, `neoforge.mods.toml`, events (`cn.li.neoforge1211.*`).
  - Version seam docs: `docs/dev/MC_VERSION_SEAM.md`. Gate: `verifyVersionSeamParity`.

- **mcmod (foundation)**
  - Clojure under `mcmod/src/main/clojure/cn/li/mcmod/...` with namespaces **`cn.li.mcmod.*`**.
  - Domain areas include: `block` (dsl, tile_dsl, tile_logic), `client` (obj, render), `events`, `gui` (api, cgui, container, core, dsl, network, …), `inventory`, `item` (dsl), `nbt` (dsl), `network`, `platform`, `registry`, `util`, etc.
  - No direct Forge/Fabric/NeoForge/Minecraft API imports; Clojure + data libs only.
  - No `src/main/resources` in this module (per `build.gradle`).

- **ac (game content)**
  - Clojure under `ac/src/main/clojure/cn/li/ac/...` with namespaces **`cn.li.ac.*`**.
  - Domains: `block`, `client/render`, `config`, `energy`, `gui`, `item`, `registry`, `terminal`, `wireless`, etc.
  - **Terminal** (`ac/.../terminal/`): server `model`, `catalog`, `player`, `network`; client `client/shell`, `client/runtime`, `client/apps`, `client/actions` (sole `requiring-resolve` entry). See `docs/04-systems/TERMINAL_SYSTEM_MAINTENANCE.md`.
  - **Wireless** (`ac/.../wireless/`): public `api`; `service.commands` / `service.queries`; `domain.topology` / `domain.transfer`; `data.world-registry` (`transact!`); `data.world` lifecycle-only. See `docs/05-wireless/WIRELESS_REFACTOR_CONTRACTS.md`.
  - **Ability** (`ac/ability/`, `ac/content/ability/`): **reducer-only** — all player-state writes via `command-runtime` → `reducer` → `runtime-store` only; `context-dispatcher` (`:as ctx`) for lifecycle/merged reads; `context-skill-state` for skill-state writes; no `context-registry` facade, no `:sync-*-data` commands, no `update-context!`. See `docs/04-systems/ABILITY_SYSTEM_MAINTENANCE.md`.
  - Depends on `mcmod`; uses mcmod DSLs/metadata; **must not** import Forge/Fabric/NeoForge/`net.minecraft.*`.
  - Shared assets: `ac/src/main/resources` (e.g. `assets/academy/`, `data/academy/`).

- **Dependency red line**
  - **`ac` / `mcmod` must not reference loader namespaces** (`cn.li.forge1201`, `cn.li.fabric1201`, `cn.li.neoforge1211`) or Minecraft version namespaces (`cn.li.mc1201`, `cn.li.mc1211`, `cn.li.mcver`).
  - Loader components must not hardcode content IDs; read metadata from `mcmod`/`ac`.
  - Minecraft components must not enumerate loaders; loader lifecycle stays under `platform-src/loader/*`.

- **Adding new content**
  - Extend DSL/metadata in **`mcmod`** when introducing new abstractions.
  - Implement gameplay in **`ac`** using `defblock` / `defitem` / etc.
  - Touch **`platform-src/loader/<target>/`** only for loader-specific wiring; keep adapters thin.
  - Cross-version Minecraft API differences go in **`cn.li.mcver`** under each `mc-<version>` component (see `docs/dev/MC_VERSION_SEAM.md`), not in `minecraft/base`.
